    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d405">

                <pb facs="0465" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg415"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Gray.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 169.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information a copy of a
                    joint resolution of Congress, approved the 15th instant, authorizing the
                    Secretary of the Treasury to permit the owners of cattle and horses which have
                    been removed into Mexico to bring the same thereafter into the United States
                    before January 15 next without charge for import duties. I inclose, also, a copy
                    of my note to the minister of Mexico here, asking him to bring the matter to the
                    attention of his Government, so that by concurrent action the full benefit of
                    the law (which expires January 14, 1895) may be enjoyed by those interested.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d405-a1.xml" xpointer="d405-a1"/>
